  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17}-15.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17}-15=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17}-15 & =0 \\\\ 5\\sqrt[4]{4x+17} & =15 \\\\ \\sqrt[4]{4x+17} & =3 \\\\ (\\sqrt[4]{4x+17})^{4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ 4x+17 & =81 \\\\ 4x & =64 \\\\ x & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\sqrt[4]{4\\cdot 16+17}-15 & =0 \\\\ 5\\sqrt[4]{81}-15 & =0 \\\\ 5\\cdot 3-15 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=16.$",
